<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Crypto Narrative Radar - {{ snapshot_date }}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f2f4f6;
      --panel: #ffffff;
      --panel-alt: #f8fafb;
      --ink: #111827;
      --muted: #5a6673;
      --line: #d4dbe3;
      --line-strong: #a9b5c3;
      --accent: #0f5f6f;
      --accent-2: #2f6f4e;
      --accent-soft: #e6f1f3;
      --terminal: #17202a;
      --warn-soft: #fff4df;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: "Aptos", "Segoe UI", "Trebuchet MS", Verdana, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .page {
      max-width: 1180px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 32px 20px 56px;
    }

    header {
      background: var(--terminal);
      border: 1px solid #23313f;
      border-radius: 6px;
      color: #f8fafc;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 34px;
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin: 34px 0 12px;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: 16px;
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .subtitle {
      color: #cbd5df;
      font-size: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .meta {
      color: #aebccc;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px;
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .notice {
      background: var(--warn-soft);
      border: 1px solid #ead5aa;
      border-radius: 6px;
      color: #514222;
      padding: 14px 16px;
    }

    .sample-notice {
      background: var(--accent-soft);
      border: 1px solid #bfdfe2;
      border-radius: 6px;
      color: #143d43;
      margin-top: 12px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
    }

    .cards {
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(245px, 1fr));
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 14px;
    }

    .card .label {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .card .value {
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 24px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 4px 0;
    }

    .card .note {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 0 0 12px 22px;
      padding: 0;
    }

    li {
      margin: 6px 0;
    }

    .table-wrap {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6px;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    table {
      border-collapse: collapse;
      min-width: 760px;
      width: 100%;
    }

    th,
    td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 9px 10px;
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    th {
      background: #edf2f5;
      color: #26333f;
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    td {
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    td,
    .card .value,
    .bar-value,
    .skew-values,
    .axis-labels {
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }

    tr:last-child td {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .section-note {
      color: var(--muted);
      max-width: 880px;
    }

    .chart-panel {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 16px;
    }

    .bar-chart,
    .skew-chart {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .bar-row,
    .skew-row {
      align-items: center;
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .bar-row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, 190px) minmax(180px, 1fr) 64px;
    }

    .bar-label,
    .skew-label {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .bar-track,
    .skew-track {
      background: var(--panel-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 4px;
      min-height: 18px;
      position: relative;
    }

    .bar-fill {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), #3f8b95);
      border-radius: 3px;
      height: 18px;
    }

    .bar-value {
      color: var(--terminal);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-align: right;
    }

    .axis-labels {
      color: var(--muted);
      display: flex;
      font-size: 12px;
      justify-content: space-between;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .skew-row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 230px) minmax(220px, 1fr) minmax(190px, 240px);
    }

    .skew-label {
      display: grid;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .review-pill {
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--muted);
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      padding: 2px 8px;
      width: fit-content;
    }

    .review-pill.skew-review,
    .review-pill.dispersion-review,
    .review-pill.skew-dispersion-review {
      background: #fff4df;
      border-color: #d7b46c;
      color: #604a13;
    }

    .review-pill.no-review {
      background: #edf7f1;
      border-color: #b8d9c6;
      color: #28543a;
    }

    .zero-line {
      background: #778494;
      bottom: -4px;
      position: absolute;
      top: -4px;
      width: 1px;
    }

    .skew-marker {
      border-radius: 999px;
      height: 14px;
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      width: 14px;
    }

    .skew-marker.mean {
      background: var(--accent);
      border: 2px solid #dff3f5;
    }

    .skew-marker.median {
      background: var(--accent-2);
      border: 2px solid #e5f3eb;
      height: 10px;
      width: 10px;
    }

    .skew-values {
      color: var(--muted);
      display: grid;
      font-size: 12px;
      gap: 2px;
    }

    .legend {
      color: var(--muted);
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      font-size: 12px;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    .legend-item {
      align-items: center;
      display: inline-flex;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .legend-dot {
      border-radius: 999px;
      display: inline-block;
      height: 9px;
      width: 9px;
    }

    .legend-dot.mean {
      background: var(--accent);
    }

    .legend-dot.median {
      background: var(--accent-2);
    }

    .method-box {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 16px;
    }

    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 12px;
      margin-top: 34px;
      padding-top: 16px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      .bar-row,
      .skew-row {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .bar-value {
        text-align: left;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="page">
    <header>
      <h1>Crypto Narrative Radar</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Static market intelligence research report using narrative-level crypto market data.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Snapshot date: {{ snapshot_date }}</span>
        <span>Generated: {{ generated_at }}</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="notice">
      <strong>Research disclaimer:</strong>
      This report is market intelligence only. It is not investment advice, contains no buy/sell recommendations,
      does not provide price prediction, does not include backtesting, and does not provide portfolio allocation guidance.
    </section>

    {% if sample_report_note %}
    <section class="sample-notice">
      {{ sample_report_note }}
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if qa_warnings %}
    <section>
      <h2>Data Quality Notes</h2>
      <ul>
        {% for warning in qa_warnings %}
        <li>{{ warning }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section>
      <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
      {% if summary.bullets %}
      <ul>
        {% for bullet in summary.bullets %}
        <li>{{ bullet }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">Executive summary metrics were not available for this snapshot.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Market Snapshot</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        {% for card in summary.cards %}
        <article class="card">
          <div class="label">{{ card.title }}</div>
          <h3>{{ card.narrative }}</h3>
          <div class="value">{{ card.value }}</div>
          <div class="note">{{ card.note }}</div>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    {% if score_chart.available %}
    <section>
      <h2>Narrative Momentum Score Bar Chart</h2>
      <p class="section-note">Narratives are sorted by the current Narrative Momentum Score. The score is a descriptive research ranking tool and does not affect any return skew diagnostics.</p>
      <div class="chart-panel">
        <div class="bar-chart">
          {% for row in score_chart.rows %}
          <div class="bar-row">
            <div class="bar-label">{{ row.primary_narrative }}</div>
            <div class="bar-track" aria-label="{{ row.primary_narrative }} {{ score_chart.score_label }} {{ row.score_label }}">
              <div class="bar-fill" style="width: {{ row.width_pct }}%;"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-value">{{ row.score_label }}</div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="axis-labels">
          <span>0</span>
          <span>100</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    {% if return_skew_chart.available %}
    <section>
      <h2>Mean vs Median 7D Return Skew Chart</h2>
      <p class="section-note">This diagnostic-only view plots mean and median 7D returns by narrative and displays the current review label. It does not affect the Narrative Momentum Score.</p>
      <div class="chart-panel">
        <div class="skew-chart">
          {% for row in return_skew_chart.rows %}
          <div class="skew-row">
            <div class="skew-label">
              <span>{{ row.primary_narrative }}</span>
              <span class="review-pill {{ row.review_flag_class }}">{{ row.review_flag }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="skew-track" aria-label="{{ row.primary_narrative }} mean {{ row.mean_label }} median {{ row.median_label }}">
              {% if return_skew_chart.zero_position_pct is not none %}
              <span class="zero-line" style="left: {{ return_skew_chart.zero_position_pct }}%;"></span>
              {% endif %}
              {% if row.mean_position_pct is not none %}
              <span class="skew-marker mean" style="left: {{ row.mean_position_pct }}%;" title="Mean 7D Return {{ row.mean_label }}"></span>
              {% endif %}
              {% if row.median_position_pct is not none %}
              <span class="skew-marker median" style="left: {{ row.median_position_pct }}%;" title="Median 7D Return {{ row.median_label }}"></span>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
            <div class="skew-values">
              <span>Mean {{ row.mean_label }}</span>
              <span>Median {{ row.median_label }}</span>
              <span>Gap {{ row.gap_label }} | IQR {{ row.iqr_label }}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="axis-labels">
          <span>{{ return_skew_chart.axis_min_label }}</span>
          <span>{{ return_skew_chart.axis_max_label }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="legend">
          <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot mean"></span>Mean 7D Return</span>
          <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot median"></span>Median 7D Return</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section>
      <h2>Narrative Ranking</h2>
      <p class="section-note">The ranking table compares narrative-level analysis across momentum, relative strength, volume confirmation, breadth of participation, and concentration context.</p>
      {% set table_data = ranking_table %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    {% if score_component_breakdown %}
    <section>
      <h2>Score Component Breakdown</h2>
      <p class="section-note">
        Component scores are percentile-rank normalized within the current narrative universe and combined into the Narrative Momentum Score. They are relative research ranking inputs, not statistical confidence.
      </p>
      {% set table_data = score_component_breakdown %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section>
      <h2>Return Skew Diagnostics</h2>
      <p class="section-note">
        This diagnostic compares mean, median, and IQR of 7D returns to show whether a narrative basket is broadly representative or influenced by one/few return outliers. It is diagnostic-only and does not affect the Narrative Momentum Score.
      </p>
      {% if return_skew_note %}
      <p class="section-note">{{ return_skew_note }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% set table_data = return_skew_diagnostics %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Return, Volume, and Breadth Review</h2>
      <p class="section-note">
        Breadth helps show whether participation is broad across a narrative. Volume confirmation helps contextualize whether market movement is supported by trading activity. These are descriptive research metrics.
      </p>
      {% set table_data = review_table %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Token-Level Contributors</h2>
      <p class="section-note">Token-level contributors show which assets are contributing most to narrative-level market activity.</p>
      {% if token_contributor_note %}
      <p class="section-note">{{ token_contributor_note }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% set table_data = token_contributors %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Concentration Review</h2>
      <p class="section-note">Concentration review shows whether narrative-level market cap is more distributed or driven by a small number of large tokens. Labels and comments are judgment-based V1 heuristics, not statistically derived cutoffs.</p>
      {% if concentration_note %}
      <p class="section-note">{{ concentration_note }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% set table_data = concentration_review %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>90-Day Historical Context</h2>
      {% if historical.available %}
      <p class="section-note">
        Historical narrative data covers {{ historical.narrative_count }} narratives from {{ historical.start_date }} to {{ historical.end_date }}. This view is descriptive trend context only.
      </p>
      {% set table_data = historical.latest_table %}
      {% if table_data %}
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <th>{{ table_data.labels.get(column, column.replace('_', ' ').title()) }}</th>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for row in table_data.rows %}
            <tr>
              {% for column in table_data.columns %}
              <td>{{ row[column]|format_value(column, table_data.formats.get(column)) }}</td>
              {% endfor %}
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% else %}
      <p class="section-note">{{ historical.note }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Methodology</h2>
      <div class="method-box">
        <p>Crypto Narrative Radar uses a manually reviewed narrative taxonomy, CoinGecko market data, token-level market snapshots, and narrative-level aggregation to create a descriptive research view.</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.score_note }} Small score gaps should be interpreted cautiously.</p>
        <p>The Narrative Momentum Score uses the current V1 framework: 40% price momentum, 25% relative strength, 20% volume confirmation, and 15% breadth of participation.</p>
        <ul>
          {% for row in methodology.score_weights %}
          <li>{{ row.weight }} {{ row.component }}: {{ row.description }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p>{{ methodology.normalization_note }}</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.relative_strength_note }}</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.concentration_note }}</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.return_skew_note }}</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.token_universe_note }}</p>
        <p>{{ methodology.taxonomy_note }}</p>
        <p>DuckDB SQL analytics outputs support narrative summaries, token-level contributors, and concentration context. Historical narrative data, when available, is used only as descriptive trend context.</p>
        <p>The score is a research ranking tool for market intelligence. It does not imply future returns.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>This report is not investment advice.</li>
        <li>It includes no buy/sell recommendations.</li>
        <li>It includes no price prediction.</li>
        <li>It includes no backtesting.</li>
        <li>It includes no portfolio allocation guidance.</li>
        <li>Snapshot and 90-day historical views are descriptive.</li>
        <li>CoinGecko data availability and API limits may affect data quality.</li>
        <li>Taxonomy design involves judgment and should be reviewed over time.</li>
        <li>No DeFiLlama fundamentals overlay is included yet.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>
      Crypto Narrative Radar static market intelligence report. Generated from existing processed outputs.
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
